    // block __fern_str_box builds: {rc@base, data@base+8, len@base+16}, with
    // box = base+8 (so box[0]=data, box[8]=len, box-8=rc). This helper is the
    // per-element step of __fern_str_arr_free and the rc-aware analogue of
    // __fern_arr_dec: rc<0 = immortal/literal (skip), rc>1 = shared (dec, keep),
    // rc==1 = sole owner (free the data buffer at size-class ceil(len/8) words
    // AND the 24-byte box at class 3), rc==0 = double free (underflow counter,
    // no heap corruption). So it is SAFE to call on any string box — including a
    // map column element that other owners still reference (it only decs) — not
    // just a compile-time-proven-unique temp. A literal's data lives below
